# Independent fixed-stage lifecycle review

The fixed source was copied before execution. Review source binding covers 34 immutable implementation/reference/document files; root's live author-verifier output and receipt files are intentionally excluded because that verifier ran in parallel. All bound source files remained stable. Modified implementation hashes: `capture-file.mjs` = `c827d4c160cb3d57ba09717396d9ac44eebabf4aeaaaa64296a3ce65d94bbfa6`; `apps/backup/restic.mjs` = `2fee91eebc98112e06034558ddd04682a96c766cb3814ffdd5a85e9f906c742e`.

The 20 focused regressions passed, zero skips/failures. They cover resolver and actual post-await stat cancellation at both former abort boundaries; post-open cancellation with handle closure; deadline before snapshot link with no snapshot/temp; deadline after link with committed success and cleaned temp/lock; data write/sync failures; primary plus temp/close cleanup errors; committed snapshot cleanup warnings; own-lock removal success/failure/missing outcomes; initializer write/sync cleanup and warning visibility; lock-writer warnings; and an exclusive-open collision that preserves a pre-existing temp. Source-bound receipt: `initial-validation.json`, SHA-256 `36e2617a5f56384294f26378705715f09437e795e73a812b4f28bedf5a82b063`.

The additional pre-commit guard consideration reproduced on three tiny synthetic lock writes. Deadline expiry after temp mkdir still allowed one open, one write and one sync. Expiry after open allowed one write and one sync. Expiry after write allowed one sync. In every case, the existing pre-link guard rejected, no lock object was published, and the temporary file was removed. Report: `precommit-deadline-observations.json`, SHA-256 `69e3ad4a1051ea066ed753efa1f3dd3bebcc67b4b699f1df19c6b0bb090f4007`.

Recommended bounded improvement: check the operation guard after awaited directory creation/open/write and before starting the next substantive temp I/O. A post-open guard stays within the created handle's cleanup scope. Close and confined temp/own-lock cleanup must still run on expiry. Keep the existing immediate pre-link check and explicit committed outcome; do not reintroduce a post-commit deadline failure. The three new diagnostics are a remaining pre-commit cooperative-deadline gap, not a failed publication regression or a claim that already pending kernel I/O can be interrupted.

One review receipt-wrapper run failed because it read UTF-8 TAP output as UTF-16. This did not change the 20 passing tests or any stage source. The exact erroneous wrapper source and a reproduced raw failure are retained as `freeze-initial.pre-encoding-fix.mjs` and `freeze-initial.failed.*`; the corrected wrapper reads UTF-8. No behavioral test threshold changed.

Fault injection changed only Node built-in API methods inside the disposable review process and restored them after each case. Owned synthetic repository and source fixtures, raw stdout/stderr and structured outcomes remain in this folder. The close-error case reports a synthetic callback error after the real handle successfully closed; it proves primary-error preservation, not behavior of a kernel close that cannot finish. No root stage, original review/stage, production or shared source was edited. Root's separate 10-test/30-original-file oracle is author evidence, not claimed as this review's execution. No full parity, security certification or performance claim is made.
